  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "V-run – turn and finish",
  "description": "A striker (A) stands with their back to goal and a defender (X) close behind, about 25 metres from a full-size goal with a keeper. A support player (B) has the ball further back, and the others queue behind B.\n\nA makes V-runs – first a few steps towards goal, then sharply back towards the ball – to create space. B always plays one touch and only moves sideways, never past A. When A gets the ball facing goal, A finishes. The defender is half-active: follows and gets in the way but does not win the ball. Rotate A → X → B → the queue.\n\nVariation: the defender goes live but may only mark from behind, and must win the ball before A has turned. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Sell the first part of the V – take the defender with you before you turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Change direction sharply and accelerate out of the turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Feel where the defender is: if you can't turn, lay it back and make a new run."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "B: play one touch and stay behind A."
    }
  ],
